# Git publishing

- The user has authorized committing and pushing completed project changes to
  `https://github.com/Laiape/autorig_tools.git` by default. Do this after the
  appropriate checks, unless the user explicitly requests local-only work.
- On this machine use `C:/proyectos/auto-rig/autorig_tools`. The parent checkout
  ignores this nested repository; checking the parent misses active changes.
  On other machines resolve the active checkout from the Maya module and Git.
- Verify the working directory, repository root, origin URL and branch before
  publishing. The current shared branch is `main`; honor explicit branch/PR
  instructions in the task.
- Include relevant code, documentation and character assets. Respect ignore
  rules for caches, credentials and temporary output; do not force-add them.
- Preserve existing local edits. Do not discard work, force-push or overwrite
  remote history. If a push fails, resolve safely or report the blocker.
- Verify the remote branch points to the published commit and report the hash.
  When there are no changes, do not create an empty commit.
